module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentAdicInternalHom
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CokernelAffineSurjectivityModuleUniverse
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.IdealPowerQuasicoherent

/-!
# The sections of an adic quotient over an affine chart, at any module universe

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_val_app_idealPowerQuotient_π` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_val_app_idealPowerQuotient_π` compute the sections of `M / 𝓘 ^ k M`
over an affine étale chart as `M(V) / 𝓘(V) ^ k M(V)`, for an `𝒪_F`-module with sections in the
universe `u` of the schemes.  This file is the same pair for a module whose sections live in an
arbitrary universe `m`, stated for the subsheaf
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerSubsheaf` — the spelling of `𝓘 ^ k M` which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleAdicQuotient` divides out, and the only one defined at a
module universe other than `u`.

The point of the generalisation is `𝓗om_{𝒪_F}(M, N)`: by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleInternalHom` the internal Hom of two `𝒪_F`-modules with
sections in `u` has its own sections in `u + 1`, so the ideal-power quotients appearing in
Stacks 08B6 are quotients of a `Modules.{u, u + 1}`, and no statement pinned to `Modules.{u, u}`
applies to them.  Nothing in the argument wants the two universes to agree.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerSubsheaf_eq_idealPowSubmodule` — the two spellings of
  `𝓘 ^ k M` agree at every module universe, both being characterised by the same chartwise
  universal property.  At `m = u` this is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_eq_idealPowSubmodule`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowerSubsheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_smallEtaleAdicQuotient` — `𝓘 ^ k M` and
  `M / 𝓘 ^ k M` are cartesian on affine charts when `M` and `𝓘` are.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_val_app_smallEtaleAdicQuotient_π` — **the projection onto
  `M / 𝓘 ^ k M` is surjective on the sections over an affine chart.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_val_app_smallEtaleAdicQuotient_π` — **its kernel there is
  `𝓘(V) ^ k · M(V)`.**

## Implementation notes

Two of the three instance arguments carried by the cokernel statements below are the
sheafification of abelian groups at the module universe and the comparison of the weak
equivalences with the locally bijective morphisms there; they are what the abelian structure of
`Modules.{u, m}` is built from, and instance search solves them at `u` and at `u + 1` alike.
They are written with the topology spelled `(smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J`, which is the
spelling instance search answers for.

The third, `HasCokernels (Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)`, is the one
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleAdicQuotient` already carries, and it is asked for here as
well rather than left to instance search.  Searching for it reduces to unifying the module
universe with the `max` pattern of `SheafOfModules.instAbelian`, and `u + 1 =?= max (u + 1) ?m`
is a universe constraint Lean reports as stuck even though `?m := u` solves it; taking the
instance as an argument means the constraint is never posted, and the instance a consumer
supplies is the same one its own `smallEtaleAdicQuotient` is built from.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08B6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08B6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03M1)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u m

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)
    (𝓘 : (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O))).Submodule)

/-- **The two spellings of `𝓘 ^ k M` agree at every module universe.**

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerSubsheaf` is the least sheaf submodule dominating the
chartwise products and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule` is the submodule with local
membership generated by them; both are characterised by containment of `𝓘(U) ^ k · M(U)` over
every chart, by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerSubsheaf_le_iff` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule_le_iff`, so each is below the other.  At the module
universe of the schemes this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_eq_idealPowSubmodule`. -/
theorem idealPowerSubsheaf_eq_idealPowSubmodule (k : ℕ) (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) :
    idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M = idealPowSubmodule 𝓘 k M := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [idealPowerSubsheaf_le_iff]
    intro U
    exact pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_chartSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 k U
  · rw [idealPowSubmodule_le_iff]
    intro X
    exact le_idealPowerSubsheaf_obj B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M X.unop

/-- **`𝓘 ^ k M` is cartesian on affine charts** when `M` and `𝓘` are, at every module
universe. -/
theorem isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowerSubsheaf
    (hIcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts 𝓘.toSheafOfModules)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hMcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts M) (k : ℕ) :
    IsCartesianOnAffineCharts
      (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M).toSheafOfModules := by
  rw [idealPowerSubsheaf_eq_idealPowSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M]
  exact isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 M hMcart hIcart k

variable [HasCokernels (Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)]
    [HasSheafify (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J AddCommGrpCat.{m}]
    [(smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{m}]

/-- **The adic quotient `M / 𝓘 ^ k M` is cartesian on affine charts** when `M` and `𝓘` are: it is
the cokernel of the inclusion of `𝓘 ^ k M`, and both of its ends are cartesian. -/
theorem isCartesianOnAffineCharts_smallEtaleAdicQuotient
    (hIcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts 𝓘.toSheafOfModules)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hMcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts M) (k : ℕ) :
    IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (cokernel (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M).ι) :=
  isCartesianOnAffineCharts_cokernel_of_cartesian'
    (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M).ι
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 hIcart M hMcart k) hMcart

/-- **The projection of `M` onto `M / 𝓘 ^ k M` is surjective on the sections over an affine
chart**, at every module universe.  This is the degree-zero form of Descent, Proposition 03DW:
the projection is an epimorphism whose source and whose kernel `𝓘 ^ k M` are cartesian on affine
charts. -/
theorem surjective_val_app_smallEtaleAdicQuotient_π
    (hIcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts 𝓘.toSheafOfModules)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hMcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts M) (k : ℕ)
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (hV : IsAffine (chartScheme V)) :
    Function.Surjective
      ((cokernel.π (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M).ι).val.app (op V)) :=
  surjective_val_app_cokernel_π_of_cartesian'
    (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M).ι
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 hIcart M hMcart k) hMcart V hV

/-- **The kernel of the projection onto `M / 𝓘 ^ k M` on the sections over an affine chart is
`𝓘(V) ^ k · M(V)`**, at every module universe.

A section dies in a sheaf quotient exactly when it is a section of the submodule divided out
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cokernel_π_app_eq_zero_iff'`), and over an affine chart the sections of
`𝓘 ^ k M` are `𝓘(V) ^ k · M(V)` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine`. -/
theorem ker_val_app_smallEtaleAdicQuotient_π
    (hIcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts 𝓘.toSheafOfModules)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hMcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts M) (k : ℕ)
    {V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (hV : IsAffine (chartScheme V)) :
    LinearMap.ker
        ((cokernel.π (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M).ι).val.app (op V)).hom =
      chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF 𝓘 V ^ k •
        (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (M.val.obj (op V))) := by
  have h : chartSubmodule B S hS F hF (idealPowerSubsheaf B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M) V =
      chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF 𝓘 V ^ k •
        (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (M.val.obj (op V))) := by
    rw [idealPowerSubsheaf_eq_idealPowSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 k M]
    exact chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine B S hS F hF 𝓘 M hMcart hIcart k hV
  refine SetLike.ext fun s => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, ← h]
  exact cokernel_π_app_eq_zero_iff' B S hS F hF _ (op V) s

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
